+
+## FINDINGS
+- [S1] src/kernel/arch/riscv64/hal/io_impl.hpp:175 — memory safety / ISA operand encoding (sfence.vma rs1 scope)
+  WHY: SFENCE.VMA all-VA scope selects on the rs1 REGISTER being x0, not on a zero value, so "r"(0ULL) materializes zero in a nonzero register and fences only VA 0x0 for the ASID — purge-before-free then leaves the freed context's other entries stale for the next holder of the recycled ASID (QEMU flushes coarsely, which is why the rv64 gates stayed green).
