+  WHY: The comment claims EL1 has no VA+ASID-combined invalidate, but TLBI VAE1 with an ASID-carrying Xt is exactly that op — the chosen context-purge superset is safe, only the rationale needs correction.
+
+## CHECK DISPOSITIONS
+1. Dynamic allocations: CLEAN — patch adds inline asm + delegates only; no new/delete/malloc.
+2. Concurrency boundaries: CLEAN — asid_free keeps its IrqGuard/live_clear shape and g_supported guard; purge runs in task context exactly where the full flush ran; no new ISR paths.
+3. Assertion masking: CLEAN — no test assertions touched in scope (test-history.txt/STATE.md out of scope).
